Factory config is an immutable Provider-specific value. `target` is required; `edgeHitTolerance` is a non-negative CSS-pixel value; and `input` controls `preventDefault` / `stopPropagation` policies separately for Pointer, Wheel, Keyboard, and Context Menu events.

## DOM and styling seam

The Provider writes geometry, stable classes, and `data-nodebraid-*` attributes, but it does not inject a runtime theme. Applications can start with minimal styles:

```css
.nodebraid-renderer-svg__node {
  fill: white;
  stroke: currentColor;
}

.nodebraid-renderer-svg__edge {
  stroke: currentColor;
}

.nodebraid-renderer-svg__connection-anchor,
.nodebraid-renderer-svg__port {
  r: 4px;
  fill: currentColor;
}

